
IMACS ACA2000
The  6th  International  Conference  on  Applications of Computer Algebra
June 25 - 28 , 2000  St. Petersburg, Russia
http://www.pdmi.ras.ru/EIMI/2000/imacs/

GENERAL CHAIR: Nikolay Vassiliev
PROGRAM CHAIRS: Victor Edneral, Richard Liska, Michael Wester
ORGANIZING COMMITTEE: Stanly Steinberg, Michael Wester, Yuri Matiyasevich, Anatoly Vershik
LOCAL COMMITTEE: Elena Novikova, Nikolay Mnev, Vyacheslav Nesterov, Sergei Slavyanov

ABOUT IMACS ACA
The meeting will focus on actual or possible applications of nontrivial 
computer algebra techniques to other fields and substantial interactions of 
computer algebra with other fields. The meeting will be run in the standard 
IMACS format where individuals are invited to organize a special session. 
Individuals can propose a special session by contacting the program chairs. 
All paper submissions must be directed to an organizer of an appropriate 
special session.

CONFERENCE TOPICS
Recent IMACS ACA conferences  have included: applications of computer 
algebra to robotics, signal processing, quantifier elimination, approximate 
algebraic computation, symbolic-numeric algorithms, combinatorial and 
computational methods  in algebraic geometry, computations in pure mathematics,
computer aided geometric design, dynamical systems and mechanics, education, 
demos of computer algebra software, applications of computer algebra to physics,
number theory, computer science, mathematics on the Internet, problem solving 
environments and other specialized  sessions.

PROPOSALS
Anyone wishing to organize a special session on IMACS ACA 2000 conference 
should send (e-mail preferred) a proposal no longer than two pages to the 
program chairs. The proposal should describe the title the proposed session 
and explain why the topic is relevant to IMACS ACA conference.  


SESSIONS OF ACA2000
* Algebraic Algorithms and Complexity 
* Celestial Mechanics and General Relativity 
* Computer Algebra Application to Involutivity and Group Analysis of 
  Differential Equations 
* Computer Algebra for Dynamical Systems and Mechanics 
* Computer Algebra Meets Education 
* Interval and Computer-Algebraic Methods in Science and Engineering 
* Problem Solving Environments 
* Approximate Algebraic Computation: towards Symbolic-Numeric Algorithms 
* Creative Mathematical and Logic Problem Solving Environment 
* Teaching of Efficient Mathematics 
* Computational Commutative and Differential Algebra 
* Association Schemes and their Applications 
* High Energy and Nuclear Physics 
* Computational Number Theory 
* Groebner Bases and Applications 
* Computer Algebra Methods in Control Systems and Applications 

Other sessions could be announced later.

You are welcome to present your contribution even in the case if 
you could not find appropriate session.
If your possible contribution concerns with general problems of
computer algebra, specialised CA software, applications of CA 
to the natural scinces, engineering and education, you can send 
the abstract of your contribution to the program committee chairs.
Please register yourself, IMACS ACA2000 web site: 
http://www.pdmi.ras.ru/~aca00/

